/-!
# Ample and very ample line bundles

Let `X` be a scheme over a field `k` and let `L` be a line bundle on `X`, that is, an invertible
sheaf of `𝒪ₓ`-modules in the sense of `WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Picard`.

* `L` is **very ample** over `k` if `X` admits an immersion `i : X ⟶ ℙ^N_k` over `k` into some
  projective space over `k` with `i^*𝒪(1) ≅ L`;
* `L` is **ample** if for every coherent sheaf `F` on `X` there is an `n₀` such that
  `F ⊗ L^{⊗n}` is generated by its global sections for every `n ≥ n₀`.

Being generated by its global sections is the third notion introduced here; for a sheaf of
modules on a site it is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, made into a `Prop` by
forgetting the choice of generating family.

The projective space used is this project's `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace`, so that the
classical `ℙ^N_k` is `ℙ(ULift (Fin (N + 1)); Spec k)`, and `𝒪(1)` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf`.

## Main definitions

- `SheafOfModules.IsGloballyGenerated`: a sheaf of modules is generated by its global
  sections.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsVeryAmple`: `L` is very ample over `k`
  (blueprint: `def:deg-ample`).
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsAmple`: `L` is ample (blueprint: `def:deg-ample`).

## Main statements

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsVeryAmple.exists_isClosedImmersion`: on a scheme
  **proper** over `k`, the immersion exhibiting a very ample line bundle is automatically a
  *closed* immersion. This is the second half of `def:deg-ample`, and is proved here.

The five permanence properties of `lem:deg-ample-basic` are *stated* here and left `sorry`;
see the implementation notes. Throughout, `Sh` abbreviates
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`.

- `Sh.IsAmple.tensorObj_of_isGloballyGenerated` and `Sh.IsAmple.tensorObj` — part (1): the
  tensor product of an ample line bundle with a globally generated one, and in particular
  with another ample one, is ample.
- `Sh.isAmple_tensorPow_iff` — part (2): for `n ≥ 1`, `L` is ample if and only if `L^{⊗n}` is.
- `Sh.IsAmple.pullback_of_isFinite` — part (3): the pullback of an ample line bundle along a
  finite morphism of proper `k`-schemes is ample.
- `Sh.isAmple_iff_exists_isVeryAmple_tensorPow` — part (4): `L` is ample if and only if some
  positive power of `L` is very ample.
- `Sh.IsAmple.exists_isVeryAmple_tensorObj_tensorPow` — part (5): if `L` is ample then
  `M ⊗ L^{⊗n}` is very ample for all `n ≫ 0`.

The two consequences of part (4) recorded in the blueprint are *derived* from it here, rather
than restated: `Sh.IsAmple.exists_isClosedImmersion`, a proper `k`-scheme carrying an ample
line bundle admits a closed immersion into a projective space over `k`, and
`Sh.isAmple_twistingSheaf_one`, `𝒪(1)` is ample on `ℙ^N_k`.

## Implementation notes

* **Deliberate `sorry`s.** The six declarations listed above under `lem:deg-ample-basic` — the
  two statements of part (1), and parts (2), (3), (4), (5) — are `sorry` by design, exactly as
  `WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.ChowLemma` states Chow's lemma without proving it. They
  are open obligations of the blueprint chapter, quoted from
  [Hartshorne, II §7] and [Kleiman, *Toward a numerical theory of ampleness*], not gaps in an
  argument given here. Part (4) in particular is a genuine theorem, not API. **Everything else
  in this file is proved**; the two consequences of part (4) are proved from it, and of course
  inherit its `sorry`. Of part (3) only the cases of a closed immersion and of an isomorphism
  are consumed downstream, but the statement is recorded for a general finite morphism, as in
  the blueprint.

* **Ampleness is not tied to a base.** `Sh.IsAmple` mentions no base field: the condition
  quantifies over coherent sheaves on `X` alone. Only very ampleness, which names a
  projective space over `k`, does. The permanence properties are nevertheless stated for
  schemes proper over `k`, since that is the generality in which they are true and the
  generality the blueprint uses.

* **Invertibility is a hypothesis, not part of the definition.** `IsAmple` and `IsVeryAmple`
  are stated for an arbitrary sheaf of modules; they are intended for line bundles, and every
  statement that needs it carries `SheafOfModules.Invertible` as a hypothesis. Note that
  `SheafOfModules.Invertible` is a `Prop`-valued definition, not a class.

* **Tensor powers.** `L^{⊗n}` is `CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory.tensorPow`, written
  `L ^⊗ n`, from `WeilConjectures.Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category`.

## References

* [Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*][hartshorne1977], II §7 and III §5.

## Blueprint

This file implements `def:deg-ample` and states `lem:deg-ample-basic` of
`curve_estimates/28_degree_of_the_isogeny.tex`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe v' u' u

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory

namespace SheafOfModules

section GloballyGenerated

variable {C : Type u'} [Category.{v'} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} R}

/-- A sheaf of modules is **generated by its global sections** if it admits a family of
generating global sections, that is, if some free sheaf of modules admits an epimorphism onto
it whose components are global sections.

This is `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` turned into a `Prop`. -/
def IsGloballyGenerated (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R) : Prop :=
  Nonempty M.GeneratingSections

/-- A sheaf of modules is generated by its global sections if and only if it is a quotient of
a free sheaf of modules. -/
theorem isGloballyGenerated_iff_exists :
    M.IsGloballyGenerated ↔ ∃ (I : Type u) (p : free I ⟶ M), Epi p := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨σ⟩
    exact ⟨σ.I, σ.π, σ.epi⟩
  · rintro ⟨I, p, hp⟩
    exact ⟨{ I := I, s := M.freeHomEquiv p, epi := by rwa [Equiv.symm_apply_apply] }⟩

/-- A quotient of a sheaf of modules generated by its global sections is generated by its
global sections. -/
theorem IsGloballyGenerated.of_epi (hM : M.IsGloballyGenerated) (p : M ⟶ N) [Epi p] :
    N.IsGloballyGenerated :=
  ⟨hM.some.ofEpi p⟩

/-- Being generated by its global sections is invariant under isomorphism. -/
theorem IsGloballyGenerated.of_iso (hM : M.IsGloballyGenerated) (e : M ≅ N) :
    N.IsGloballyGenerated :=
  hM.of_epi e.hom

/-- Being generated by its global sections is invariant under isomorphism. -/
theorem isGloballyGenerated_congr (e : M ≅ N) :
    M.IsGloballyGenerated ↔ N.IsGloballyGenerated :=
  ⟨fun hM ↦ hM.of_iso e, fun hN ↦ hN.of_iso e.symm⟩

/-- A free sheaf of modules is generated by its global sections. -/
theorem isGloballyGenerated_free (I : Type u) :
    (free (R := R) I).IsGloballyGenerated :=
  ⟨free.generatingSections I⟩

variable (R) in
/-- The structure sheaf is generated by its global sections. -/
theorem isGloballyGenerated_unit : (unit R).IsGloballyGenerated :=
  (isGloballyGenerated_free (R := R) PUnit.{u + 1}).of_iso
    (coproductUniqueIso (fun _ : PUnit.{u + 1} ↦ unit R))

end GloballyGenerated

end SheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

section Ample

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A sheaf of `𝒪ₓ`-modules `L` is **ample** if for every coherent sheaf `F` on `X` there is an
`n₀` such that `F ⊗ L^{⊗n}` is generated by its global sections for every `n ≥ n₀`.

This is intended for a line bundle `L`; invertibility is not part of the definition, and is
carried as a hypothesis by the statements that need it.
(blueprint: `def:deg-ample`) -/
def IsAmple (L : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∀ F : X.Modules, F.IsCoherent →
    ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ n ≥ n₀, SheafOfModules.IsGloballyGenerated (F ⊗ L ^⊗ n)

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]

/-- A sheaf of `𝒪ₓ`-modules `L` on a scheme `X` over a field `k` is **very ample** over `k` if
there is an `N` and an immersion `i : X ⟶ ℙ^N_k` over `k` with `i^*𝒪(1) ≅ L`.

This is intended for a line bundle `L`; it is one automatically as soon as such an `i` exists,
since `𝒪(1)` is one by `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.invertible_twistingSheaf` and
pullback preserves line bundles.
(blueprint: `def:deg-ample`) -/
def IsVeryAmple (L : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∃ (N : ℕ) (i : X ⟶ ℙ(ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1)); Spec (.of k))),
    IsImmersion i ∧ i.IsOver (Spec (.of k)) ∧
      Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj
        (ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf (ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1))) (Spec (.of k)) 1) ≅ L)

variable {k}
variable {L M : X.Modules}

/-- Very ampleness is invariant under isomorphism. -/
theorem IsVeryAmple.of_iso (hL : IsVeryAmple k L) (e : L ≅ M) : IsVeryAmple k M := by
  obtain ⟨N, i, hi, hio, ⟨e'⟩⟩ := hL
  exact ⟨N, i, hi, hio, ⟨e' ≪≫ e⟩⟩

/-- A very ample sheaf of modules is invertible: it is the pullback of `𝒪(1)`, which is a line
bundle, and pullback preserves line bundles. -/
theorem IsVeryAmple.invertible (hL : IsVeryAmple k L) : L.Invertible := by
  obtain ⟨_, i, _, _, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hL
  exact (SheafOfModules.Invertible.pullback i
    (ProjectiveSpace.invertible_twistingSheaf _ _ 1)).of_iso e

/-- **On a proper `k`-scheme, a very ample line bundle is cut out by a closed immersion**: the
immersion into projective space exhibiting `L` as very ample is automatically a closed
immersion, since `X` is proper over `k` and `ℙ^N_k` is separated over `k`.
(blueprint: second bullet of `def:deg-ample`) -/
theorem IsVeryAmple.exists_isClosedImmersion [IsProper (X ↘ Spec (.of k))]
    (hL : IsVeryAmple k L) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (i : X ⟶ ℙ(ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1)); Spec (.of k))),
      IsClosedImmersion i ∧ i.IsOver (Spec (.of k)) ∧
        Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback i).obj
          (ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf (ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1))) (Spec (.of k)) 1) ≅ L) := by
  obtain ⟨N, i, hi, hio, he⟩ := hL
  exact ⟨N, i, IsClosedImmersion.of_isImmersion_over i (Spec (.of k)), hio, he⟩

end Ample

section Permanence

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] {X : Scheme.{u}} [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
  [IsProper (X ↘ Spec (.of k))] {L M : X.Modules}

/-- **The tensor product of an ample line bundle with a globally generated one is ample.**
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (1))

`sorry` by design: this is quoted from the literature, see the implementation notes. -/
theorem IsAmple.tensorObj_of_isGloballyGenerated (hL : L.Invertible) (hM : M.Invertible)
    (hLa : L.IsAmple) (hMg : M.IsGloballyGenerated) :
    (L ⊗ M).IsAmple :=
  sorry

/-- **The tensor product of two ample line bundles is ample.**
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (1))

`sorry` by design: this is quoted from the literature, see the implementation notes. -/
theorem IsAmple.tensorObj (hL : L.Invertible) (hM : M.Invertible)
    (hLa : L.IsAmple) (hMa : M.IsAmple) :
    (L ⊗ M).IsAmple :=
  sorry

/-- **A positive power of a line bundle is ample if and only if the bundle is.**
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (2))

`sorry` by design: this is quoted from the literature, see the implementation notes. -/
theorem isAmple_tensorPow_iff (hL : L.Invertible) {n : ℕ} (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    (L ^⊗ n).IsAmple ↔ L.IsAmple :=
  sorry

/-- **Ampleness is preserved by pullback along a finite morphism of proper `k`-schemes.**
Downstream only the cases of a closed immersion and of an isomorphism are used.
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (3))

`sorry` by design: this is quoted from the literature, see the implementation notes. -/
theorem IsAmple.pullback_of_isFinite {X' : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    [IsProper (X' ↘ Spec (.of k))] (u : X' ⟶ X) [IsFinite u] [u.IsOver (Spec (.of k))]
    (hL : L.Invertible) (hLa : L.IsAmple) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback u).obj L).IsAmple :=
  sorry

/-- **A line bundle is ample if and only if some positive power of it is very ample.**
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (4))

`sorry` by design: this is a genuine theorem, not API; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem isAmple_iff_exists_isVeryAmple_tensorPow (hL : L.Invertible) :
    L.IsAmple ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, 1 ≤ n ∧ IsVeryAmple k (L ^⊗ n) :=
  sorry

/-- **A high tensor power of an ample line bundle makes any line bundle very ample.**
(blueprint: `lem:deg-ample-basic` (5))

`sorry` by design: this is quoted from the literature, see the implementation notes. -/
theorem IsAmple.exists_isVeryAmple_tensorObj_tensorPow (hL : L.Invertible) (hM : M.Invertible)
    (hLa : L.IsAmple) :
    ∃ n₀ : ℕ, ∀ n ≥ n₀, IsVeryAmple k (M ⊗ L ^⊗ n) :=
  sorry

/-- **A proper `k`-scheme carrying an ample line bundle is projective**: it admits a closed
immersion over `k` into a projective space over `k`.
(blueprint: first consequence of `lem:deg-ample-basic` (4)) -/
theorem IsAmple.exists_isClosedImmersion (hL : L.Invertible) (hLa : L.IsAmple) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (i : X ⟶ ℙ(ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1)); Spec (.of k))),
      IsClosedImmersion i ∧ i.IsOver (Spec (.of k)) := by
  obtain ⟨n, -, hn⟩ := (isAmple_iff_exists_isVeryAmple_tensorPow k hL).1 hLa
  obtain ⟨N, i, hi, hio, -⟩ := hn.exists_isClosedImmersion
  exact ⟨N, i, hi, hio⟩

end Permanence

/-- **`𝒪(1)` is ample on `ℙ^N_k`**: it is very ample, being the pullback of itself along the
identity immersion.
(blueprint: second consequence of `lem:deg-ample-basic` (4)) -/
theorem isAmple_twistingSheaf_one (k : Type u) [Field k] (N : ℕ) :
    (ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf (ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1))) (Spec (.of k)) 1).IsAmple := by
  set n := ULift.{u} (Fin (N + 1))
  set P := ℙ(n; Spec (.of k))
  have hveryample : IsVeryAmple k (ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf n (Spec (.of k)) 1) :=
    ⟨N, 𝟙 P, inferInstance, inferInstance,
      ⟨(Scheme.Modules.pullbackId P).app (ProjectiveSpace.twistingSheaf n (Spec (.of k)) 1)⟩⟩
  refine (isAmple_iff_exists_isVeryAmple_tensorPow k
    (ProjectiveSpace.invertible_twistingSheaf n (Spec (.of k)) 1)).2 ⟨1, le_rfl, ?_⟩
  exact hveryample.of_iso (tensorPowOneIso _).symm

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
